@startuml command_class_diagram
title Wzorzec Polecenie - diagram klas (GoF)

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho

interface Command {
    + Execute()
    + Undo()
}

class ConcreteCommand {
    - _receiver: Receiver
    - _prevState
    + Execute()
    + Undo()
}

class Invoker {
    - _command: Command
    + SetCommand(Command)
    + ExecuteCommand()
    + UndoCommand()
}

class Receiver {
    + Action()
    + ReverseAction()
}

class Client {
    <<creates>>
}

Command <|.. ConcreteCommand
ConcreteCommand --> Receiver : receiver.Action()
Invoker o--> Command : <<uses>>
Client ..> ConcreteCommand : <<creates>>
Client ..> Receiver : <<creates>>
Client ..> Invoker : <<configures>>

note right of Invoker
  Invoker nie wie, co robi Command.
  Zna tylko interfejs Command.
end note

note right of ConcreteCommand
  Łączy Receiver z konkretną akcją.
  Przechowuje stan potrzebny do Undo.
end note

note bottom of Receiver
  Receiver zawiera faktyczną
  logikę biznesową.
end note

@enduml
